    "body": "Host Checklist Role: Host Updated: May 2026 Category: FOH Operations The host is the first and last impression every guest has of the restaurant. The room must be perfect before a single guest arrives. Work through this checklist before doors open and submit at the end of your shift. 1. Opening — Room & Entrance Front of House Unlock and inspect guest entrance — no debris, stains, or obstructions outside Host stand is stocked — menus, pens, reservation system, seating chart Check coat area or waiting area is clean, clear, and ready Walk every table — wobbles, crumbs, uneven settings, and dirty glassware all need fixing before service Check lights, music level, and temperature — all set to house standard Restrooms inspected, stocked with soap and paper towels, clean, dry, and logged before doors open Menus Menus are clean — no sticky covers, torn pages, or outdated inserts Enough menus for expected covers plus 20% buffer Any menus with allergen inserts or specials are updated for today 2. Reservations & Pre-Service Brief Review all reservations — confirm names, party sizes, times, and table assignments Flag VIP guests, special occasions, and birthdays — brief servers on each one Read every allergy note in the reservation system aloud to the team in the pre-service brief Identify accessibility needs — wheelchair access, hearing, seating preferences Note any large parties and confirm with the kitchen on pacing and timing Confirm the seating plan and section assignments with manager before service 3. During Service Door & Seating Greet every guest within 30 seconds of entering — eye contact, name if reservation known Walk-ins are quoted accurate wait times — do not underquote to please Pace seatings with the kitchen — do not flood sections back-to-back Escort guests to the table — do not point and direct Allergen guests: verbally confirm allergy with server at handoff — do not leave it to the guest to repeat Floor Monitoring Check restrooms every 30–45 minutes during service — restock and clean as needed Monitor waiting area — update guests on wait times proactively Alert manager immediately if a guest is becoming agitated or a wait is running significantly long 4. End of Shift Reset host stand — menus restocked, system closed correctly, pens returned Final restroom check — cleaned, stocked, and logged Log any guest complaints, incidents, or accessibility issues for manager review Note any large parties, VIPs, or special setups for the following day's opening team Confirm tomorrow's reservations are visible in the system before leaving Submit Checklist Submit at the end of your shift. Logged automatically in the manager's Google Sheet. Submit Host Checklist Related Host Role Guide Greeting & Seating SOP Reservations & Waitlist SOP Allergen Communication SOP Full FOH Opening Checklist"
