    "body": "Line Cook Checklist Role: Line Cook Updated: May 2026 Category: BOH Operations Your station is your responsibility from the moment you arrive to the moment you hand it off. Station setup, food safety during service, and end-of-shift clean-down are all yours. Submit your checklist at the end of each shift. 1. Station Setup — Before Service Hygiene Wash hands before touching anything on the line Sanitize station surfaces, boards, and immediate prep area before setting up Confirm color-coded boards are correct for your station — no cross-contamination Clean uniform on, hair tied back or covered, no jewellery or nail varnish Station Readiness Check all station items are within date and correctly labelled Confirm hot-hold is heating — target 140 F before service Confirm grill, fryer, or oven is at correct service temperature Check utensils, backup pans, towels, and liners are in place Probe thermometer is sanitized, calibrated, and at your station Service Brief Read the 86 list — know what you cannot send out today Know today's specials, pickups, and any modified allergen dishes Know who is calling tickets and who is running food 2. During Service Food Safety Probe every high-risk protein before it leaves the station — poultry 165 F, fish 145 F, minced meat 165 F Probe reheated items before placing in hot-hold — minimum 165 F throughout Never judge doneness by color — the probe is the only check Sanitize probe between each protein type Any food out of temperature — stop service and tell the manager immediately Allergen Tickets Every allergen-flagged ticket requires the Allergen Handling SOP — clean board, dedicated utensils, verbal pass confirmation Never assume a dish is allergen-safe — check the recipe, check the ticket Call out the allergen aloud when handing to the pass Station Hygiene Keep station clear — no build-up of debris or spills during service Wash hands after touching raw proteins, face, phone, or leaving the kitchen Any cut — stop, clean, cover with blue detectable plaster, rewash hands before continuing 3. End of Shift Cover and label every item remaining on your station — name, prep date, use-by date Any hot food remaining must be cooled correctly before refrigerating — ice bath first Sanitize all station surfaces and boards Return all knives to the magnetic strip Clear and clean hot-hold equipment and empty any unused product Note any low stock, equipment issues, or quality problems for the closer or manager Submit Checklist Submit at the end of each shift. Logged automatically in the manager's Google Sheet. Submit Line Cook Checklist Log any temperature readings or corrective actions in the Daily Temperature Log as they happen — not at the end of your shift. Related Daily Temperature Log Line Cook Role Guide Allergen Handling SOP Temperature Logging SOP Corrective Action SOP"
