    "body": "Prep Cook Checklist Role: Prep Cook Updated: May 2026 Category: BOH Operations Prep drives service. Everything you produce must be labelled the moment it leaves your hands, stored correctly, and ready on time. Work through this checklist at the start and end of every prep shift. 1. Prep Station Setup Hygiene First Wash hands before touching any food or equipment Sanitize all cutting boards and prep surfaces before setting up Confirm color-coded boards are correct — red for raw red meat, yellow for poultry, blue for fish, green for produce, white for dairy and cooked Set sanitizer spray bottle and paper towel at station — test strip confirms correct concentration Stock Audit Pull today's prep list from manager before touching any product Inspect all prepped items from yesterday — check label, date, and condition Discard anything past its use-by date — do not re-label or guess Rotate new stock FIFO — new deliveries go behind existing stock Flag any low stock, missing product, or quality issues to manager before starting prep Station Equipment Scale is zeroed and clean Deli cups, labels, permanent marker, and lids are at the station Probe thermometer available and sanitized for checking hot prep 2. During Prep Labelling — No Exceptions Label every prepped item the moment it is finished — item name, prep date, use-by date Write labels in permanent marker — legible and on the container, not the lid No unlabelled containers in the fridge, ever Cooling Hot Prep Never put hot food directly into the fridge — always ice-bath first Use shallow containers no deeper than 3 inches Cool from above 140 F to below 70 F within 2 hours, then to 41 F or below within 4 hours total Probe the centre of cooling batches — log the reading on the daily temperature log If food has not reached 41 F within 4 hours, discard it and notify manager Cross-Contamination Sanitize board and knife between each protein type Never use the same board for raw protein and produce without sanitizing first If an allergen-free batch is required, use the purple dedicated board and clean utensils Wash hands every time you switch between protein types 3. End of Prep Shift All completed prep is labelled, covered, and stored in the correct fridge location Any remaining hot product is ice-bathed and cooling correctly before you leave Sanitize all prep surfaces and boards Return all equipment — scales, containers, deli lids — to their storage locations Note any prep items not completed and tell the manager or opener before leaving Submit Checklist Submit at the end of your prep shift. Logged automatically in the manager's Google Sheet. Submit Prep Cook Checklist Log any cooling temperature readings in the Daily Temperature Log as they happen during prep. Related Daily Temperature Log Prep Cook Role Guide Cold Prep Setup SOP Cooling & Reheating SOP Date Labelling SOP Color Coding SOP"
