    "body": "Reservations & Waitlist Role: Host Category: FOH SOP Updated: May 2026 Step 1 Record complete booking notes Every booking must include name, phone, party size, time, date, special occasions, allergies, accessibility needs, and seating requests. Repeat the booking back before ending the call or confirming online changes. Step 2 Quote wait times honestly Quote a range, not a promise. Use the table plan, kitchen pacing, and current dessert/payment stage to estimate. If the wait changes by more than 10 minutes, update the guest before they ask. Step 3 Manage table turns without rushing guests Watch course stage, bill stage, and reservation times. Alert the manager early if a table will not turn on time. Do not pressure guests directly unless the manager instructs you how to phrase it. Step 4 Communicate handoffs When seating from a waitlist, tell the server if the guest waited a long time, has a deadline, has allergies, or is celebrating. Mark the table seated and remove the guest from the waitlist immediately. Related Greeting & Seating FOH Opening FOH Home"
